HOW REAL AIRCRAFT DETECTS IT 

                         Windshear detection
                                 │
             ┌───────────────────┴────────────────────┐
        PREDICTIVE (PWS)                          REACTIVE
        = weather radar                           = flight computer
        sees it AHEAD (before you enter)          feels it when you're IN it
             │                                         │
   Doppler: measures drop speed               measures airspeed loss, sinking
   drops coming TOWARDS on one side           → "WINDSHEAR WINDSHEAR WINDSHEAR"
   drops going AWAY on the other side         → red WINDSHEAR on PFD
             │                                → pilot: full power, pitch up
   calculates F-FACTOR (how fast you'd
   lose energy). 0.13 or more = danger
             │
   only below 2300 ft, 5 NM ahead
   amber: "Monitor radar display"
   red:   "Go around, windshear ahead"
          "Windshear ahead" (takeoff)



