A microburst is a type of windshear. It forms when cold, heavy air falls out of a storm and spreads out along the ground. It lasts 5–15 minutes in real weather. Radar can detect it because of the rain drops in it.
In my app the PWS works below 2300 ft. From 2300 to 1200 ft it shows only the icon. Below 1200 ft it gives an alert: amber if the microburst is far or to the side, red if it is close and straight ahead.
It is most dangerous near the ground because the plane is slow and low, with no height left to recover.



